    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the hearth is almost out, just like everything else. I'm sitting here in the dust of what used to be a throne room, looking at my hands... they're stained with things I can't wash off. There's no more battles to fight, no more people to protect. Even the ghosts have stopped whispering. I feel like I'm just... waiting for the air to run out. There's nothing left of the man I was, and nothing left for the man I am. The silence is just too heavy now.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
